WEBVTT

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:04.710
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:10.250
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:15.540
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:31.180
I’m back!

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:34.420
I’m back, Wanpachi.

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:36.220
Come on out, Eevee.

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:43.320
Thanks for waiting!

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.070
Have you been a good boy?

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:57.700
What is it, Eevee?

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:59.390
Welcome back, Koharu.

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:00.960
I’m back, Dad.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.920
Can you come here a moment?

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:08.170
Welcome back, Koharu.

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:09.800
Nice timing!

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:11.820
What is it?

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:16.810
Hey! Have you been
finding fossils <i>enchanting?</i>

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:19.680
The president of
the Museum of Science?

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.820
Apparently he has a request for you.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:23.690
About investigating fossils!

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:26.360
In the Wild Area! The Wild Area!

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:27.730
Over in Galar?

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:29.440
<i>Indeeding!</i>

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:34.070
You can find rare fossils in Galar,
according to a rumor I heard.

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:38.410
I’d like you to go and investigate
what these rare fossils are like!

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:39.960
I’ll do it!

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:41.710
Me, too!

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:46.180
I can meet lots of Pokémon
in the Wild Area! Right, Aceburn?!

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.230
What will you do, Koharu?

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:51.490
I have school, so...

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:55.560
You want to go?

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:05.400
Dad, I want to go too!

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:13.530
Satoshi and Go left for Galar to investigate the fossils...
and Koharu went along, too.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:17.760
Now, what sort of encounters
and adventures await them?

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:20.520
What’re you looking at?

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:22.560
An e-mail from the teacher.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:26.920
She’s asking me to write a report about the trip
to make up for missing lessons.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:28.460
Huh, that’s great!

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:29.260
Yeah!

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:37.760
All you can see is clouds...

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:30.210
The Wild Area, Galar Region

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.800
Aceburn, go!

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:53.270
Whoa!
There’s so many Pokémon!

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:10.460
What? Um... What’s that...?

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:16.050
Gantle. Ore Pokémon.
Rock-type.

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:17.880
It relies on sound to
monitor its vicinity.

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:22.220
When angered, it will attack
without ever changing the direction it’s facing.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:25.550
Eevee!

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:28.480
Aceburn! Blaze Kick!

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:35.230
Harden, huh?

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:37.190
Aceburn!
Lightning Speed!

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:44.870
Monster Ball, go!

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:58.210
Gantle’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:00.660
All right, Gantle caught!

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:03.680
Great!

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:05.840
Go! Thank you!

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:07.990
And you, Aceburn!

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.890
Now, let’s go!

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:11.750
Yes!

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:14.220
Wait for me!

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:20.150
You get that.

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:27.920
This must be it!
Okay, time to dig!

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:30.960
Aceburn!
Let’s get stuck in together!

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:33.300
We should go too, Pikachu!

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:35.670
Eevee!
We’ll look for fossils, too!

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:37.920
Banbadoro! Double Kick!

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:39.670
Eevee!

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:41.270
Pikachu! Iron Tail!

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:46.350
You okay?

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:48.130
Yeah! Thank you!

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:51.680
Oh, somebody there?
Sorry ‘bout that.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:54.140
What’s with that
“Sorry ‘bout that”?!

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:59.020
I’m Gasattsu.
Here to dig up fossils.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:02.530
You lookin’ for fossils too?

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:03.180
Yeah!

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:05.550
We heard we could
find rare fossils here...

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:06.910
Okay, this way.

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:14.930
What is this?

00:07:14.930 --> 00:07:16.810
A hand? A foot?

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:19.570
Is this... a tail?

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:21.050
Ain’t they great?

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:23.400
This isn’t a complete fossil,
am I right?

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:29.230
Right. But dig here and there,
and we’ll <i>probably</i> find the whole thing eventually.

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:31.220
I see you’re as rough as ever.

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:33.180
You took your time. You’re late!

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:37.060
Well, I forgot to
set my alarm clock...

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:38.540
You’re so careless...

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:39.670
Who’s that?

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:41.560
A fellow researcher, Ukattsu.

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:42.920
Hello!

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:44.260
Hello.

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:47.560
Ukattsu,
let’s get the investigation started.

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:48.960
Got it.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:53.700
I forgot my pickaxe!

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:56.270
You’re so careless... Here.

00:07:57.290 --> 00:07:59.760
Um... We can help, too!

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:02.170
It’ll go faster if we’re all digging!

00:08:02.170 --> 00:08:03.910
That would help.

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:05.800
Can we ask for your help, then?

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:07.430
Yeah!

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:13.190
This is heavy...

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:19.470
You’ve got it!

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:25.660
What’s this?!

00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:29.260
Looks like a fossil of a foot.
Isn’t that great?

00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:31.510
Eevee! You did a great job!

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:40.880
How do these fit together?

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:43.490
I’m not even sure
which way they face.

00:08:43.490 --> 00:08:45.210
It’s like some sort of puzzle.

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:48.820
That’s the mysterious thing
about Galar’s fossils.

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:50.060
Mysterious?

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:56.820
I think the right answer might just be some odd match-up
that completely defies all prior ideas!

00:08:57.710 --> 00:08:59.690
Here’s my prediction.

00:08:59.690 --> 00:09:03.120
This, and this make one Pokémon.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:09.570
This area used to be a seabed. So it would’ve needed
limbs that can move through water easily.

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:15.290
And since it swam deep in the ocean, this Pokémon
needed a physiology that could eat prey above it.

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:18.080
I named it Uochilldon!

00:09:19.060 --> 00:09:20.250
I was just thinking...

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:24.240
I’d match up this one and this one.

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:26.120
My hypothesis is...

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:29.530
This area was plains,
with nothing but short shrubs.

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:35.230
So bird Pokémon would need to run more than they fly,
ending up with a stronger lower body.

00:09:35.230 --> 00:09:38.140
Like this!
I named it Pacchiragon!

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:39.140
Ooh!

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:42.000
Looks like it could be right,
or just as easily be wrong...

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:43.850
It really is mysterious...

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:48.260
We’ve found all the fossils we need.
Why don’t we restore them straight away?!

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:49.360
Yeah.

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:56.320
This one isn’t shutting properly.

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:59.210
Hey, be more careful with that.

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:01.000
Okay, it’s shut.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:02.960
You’re so rough with things...

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:06.420
My Pacchiragon is...
this one and this one.

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:11.510
Huh? Wasn’t that my Uochilldon?
I’m sure it was blue...

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:15.510
No! Mine was blue.
Yours is light blue.

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:18.760
Huh? Light blue?
I thought it was the blue one...

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:22.520
Well, they’re pretty much the same thing!
Hurry up and get the machine!

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:26.770
Ta-daah!
This is the fossil restoration device!

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:32.270
With this, we can restore the fossil pieces
to their original form.

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:33.960
Amazing, right?

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:36.180
The principle is
the same as Monster Balls.

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:37.130
They’re turned into light—

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:39.760
Don’t bother with the explanation.
Nobody gets it anyway.

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:40.740
Ugh!

00:10:41.190 --> 00:10:44.330
The withdraw button... On!

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:54.700
All right.

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:56.440
Now I just press
the emerge button...

00:10:56.440 --> 00:10:57.900
No, the restore button!

00:10:57.900 --> 00:10:59.180
Oh, whoops.

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:00.430
You’re so careless...

00:11:03.270 --> 00:11:07.700
Now the fossil pieces will be
converted to light particles and reconstructed...

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:11.220
Or more simply,
put together like a puzzle...

00:11:11.220 --> 00:11:14.030
Then they’ll appear,
fully restored!

00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:17.730
So, how long will that take?

00:11:17.730 --> 00:11:20.470
Two hours.
No, maybe four hours.

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:22.630
What should we do
while we wait?

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:25.790
How about making
something to eat?

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:27.000
I’m in!

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:28.690
Great idea! A camp meal!

00:11:28.690 --> 00:11:30.130
What should we make?!

00:11:30.130 --> 00:11:33.010
When you cook in the Wild Area,
you’ve gotta have...

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:34.130
Curry!

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:36.840
Let’s make a great curry together!

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:38.510
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:44.480
Do you think this looks good?

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:47.980
Don’t worry! It just needs to be hot enough
to dissolve everything!

00:11:47.980 --> 00:11:48.690
Right!

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:51.690
Momon berries and Mago berries...

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:54.940
Huh, so if you grind them enough,
they have a milder taste!

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:58.160
Don’t worry!
Cook it enough and it’ll all dissolve!

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:01.410
That’s how you have hafta make
Wild Area curry!

00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:05.140
Make sure you stir it properly
so it doesn’t burn, okay?

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:06.380
I know!

00:12:06.380 --> 00:12:08.080
You’re so rough...

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:09.590
Where’s the curry roux?!

00:12:09.590 --> 00:12:11.420
I brought it.
Look over there.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:14.920
Huh? That’s chocolate...

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:17.880
Oh, no! I mixed them up!

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:20.010
You’re so careless...

00:12:24.350 --> 00:12:26.620
Oh, sorry, Eevee.

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:33.190
I’m making a tasty dessert with some Moomoo Milk,
so just wait a bit longer, okay?

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:38.580
Hmm... Now for some sugar...

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:41.810
For a curry, you need
some kind of secret ingredient...

00:12:41.810 --> 00:12:44.490
We could do with one of those,
but what...?

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:49.160
I’ve got it!

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:52.280
Huh?
Where’s the whipped cream?

00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:55.440
Go! Have you seen it?

00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:56.600
I haven’t!

00:12:56.600 --> 00:12:58.300
I wonder where it went...

00:12:58.300 --> 00:13:01.510
And it’s done!
Special whipped cream curry!

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:04.290
What is this...?

00:13:04.290 --> 00:13:05.760
That was my...

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:08.130
I used it as the
secret ingredient!

00:13:08.130 --> 00:13:10.680
Um, it’s...
hardly “secret”...

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:12.550
<i>So rough...</i>

00:13:12.550 --> 00:13:15.190
Well, why don’t we just try it.

00:13:15.190 --> 00:13:17.860
<i>H-Here g-goes...</i>

00:13:24.890 --> 00:13:26.580
<i>Delicious!</i>

00:13:28.330 --> 00:13:29.930
It’s pretty good, isn’t it?

00:13:29.930 --> 00:13:31.870
It’s not bad.

00:13:32.610 --> 00:13:34.750
We’re finished!

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:36.540
We sure ate...

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:39.890
My belly hurts...

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:42.550
You had too many extra servings...

00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:44.540
What’s that?

00:13:44.540 --> 00:13:46.560
The fossil restoration is complete!

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:47.740
Really?

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:49.200
Great!

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:51.690
Okay, out they come.

00:13:51.690 --> 00:13:54.210
Don’t press the wrong thing.
It’s the emerge button, remember?

00:13:54.210 --> 00:13:55.150
Right, right...

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:10.190
Pocket Monsters!

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:34.900
Whoa!
They were really restored!

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:38.770
But don’t they look different
to the predictions?

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:40.190
Yeah...

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:43.790
And that’s the mysterious thing
about Galar’s fossils!

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:45.240
Huh?

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:50.240
It doesn’t quite match my hypothesis,
but look what potential they had!

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:53.210
I’ll call it Pacchilldon!

00:14:53.720 --> 00:15:00.260
It lived in the ancient seas,
and must have chilled and stored its prey with its icy body!

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:04.430
That hypothesis
changed quite a bit...

00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:07.390
What’s this?

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:10.730
Well, those are Galar’s fossils.
Aren’t they mysterious...?

00:15:10.730 --> 00:15:12.850
If I had to name it... Right!

00:15:13.320 --> 00:15:14.960
Uonoragon!

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:22.420
With its powerful legs and jaws,
it was unrivaled on land!

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:25.380
But it overhunted its prey,
and went extinct.

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:27.710
Yeah, that has to be
what happened!

00:15:27.710 --> 00:15:30.760
Huh! Nice to meet you,
Uonoragon!

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:33.500
That was close.

00:15:35.630 --> 00:15:37.580
Why?!

00:15:41.470 --> 00:15:43.200
Looks like it likes him.

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:44.650
Are you sure about that?

00:15:44.650 --> 00:15:46.050
It won’t stop...

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:48.720
Pikachu! Electroweb!

00:15:57.230 --> 00:15:58.220
Dodge it!

00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:15.250
Satoshi!

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:24.630
Oh, dear!

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:27.880
Aceburn, melt the ice
with Pyro Ball!

00:16:43.010 --> 00:16:44.790
Thank you, Eevee!

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:46.700
You okay, Koharu?

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:47.710
Yeah!

00:16:47.710 --> 00:16:49.740
I need to calm it down!

00:16:53.830 --> 00:16:56.910
How far are you gonna run?!

00:16:59.340 --> 00:17:01.780
Gantle, go!

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:06.870
I’m counting on you, Gantle!

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:18.310
Stop running, Uonorago—

00:17:39.420 --> 00:17:40.410
So cold...

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:42.140
Are you okay?

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:43.750
We’ll manage...

00:17:44.420 --> 00:17:47.460
Why isn’t it moving?

00:17:48.890 --> 00:17:50.880
That’s... Charge!

00:17:56.960 --> 00:17:57.720
Here it comes!

00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:14.950
So... you just wanted to swim?

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:20.120
I see!

00:18:20.690 --> 00:18:23.400
Hey, why don’t we go
have a look around?

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:32.510
Gantle! Harden!

00:18:38.270 --> 00:18:40.140
Gantle! Stone Edge!

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:53.990
It managed to withstand that?
It’s got some guts!

00:18:53.990 --> 00:18:55.360
Look out!

00:18:56.790 --> 00:18:57.440
Stop!

00:18:57.440 --> 00:18:58.780
Huh? Satoshi?

00:18:58.780 --> 00:18:59.830
Move!

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:07.210
Are you okay?

00:19:08.140 --> 00:19:10.050
That was a shock...

00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:13.740
You’re not hurt anywhere?

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:16.310
Stop it...

00:19:20.020 --> 00:19:22.540
All right.
Looks like it’s calmed down.

00:19:22.540 --> 00:19:23.430
Yeah!

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:26.530
Looks like it likes you.

00:19:26.530 --> 00:19:27.960
Are you okay?

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:30.800
Thanks to you. Thank you.

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:34.910
So hey, what do you think?

00:19:34.910 --> 00:19:38.030
Would you look after
these fossil Pokémon?

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:39.170
Huh?

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:40.250
We can?

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:45.550
Sure! We have our new data now,
so we’re satisfied. Right?

00:19:45.550 --> 00:19:46.750
Yeah!

00:19:47.150 --> 00:19:49.920
Pacchilldon!
Will you come with me?

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:54.350
Let’s be friends,
Uonoragon!

00:19:57.100 --> 00:19:59.310
Monster Ball, go!

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:12.190
Pacchilldon’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:16.950
Uonoragon’s data will be
added to the Index.

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:18.400
Uonoragon...

00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:19.610
Pacchilldon...

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:21.440
I’ve caught you!

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:26.270
You’re both amazing!

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:36.780
I see!
Pacchilldon and Uonoragon...

00:20:36.780 --> 00:20:39.300
They’re truly mysterious
fossil Pokémon!

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:41.800
Aren’t they just <i>enchanting?</i>

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:44.230
Thank you very much
for your report.

00:20:44.230 --> 00:20:45.180
Sure!

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:46.280
Bye then!

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:52.560
So, how was it?

